# [TLS](../wg/tls.html)

## Summary

The TLS Working Group held its first session at IETF 127. The working group reviewed document status, addressed DTLS 1.3 `ClientHello` fragmentation issues for post-quantum key shares, evaluated updates to Trust Anchor Identifiers, received an update on the Password Authenticated Key Exchange (PAKE) extension, and debated a proposal for Workload Identifier origin hints in mTLS.

## Key Discussion Points

### Working Group Status
- **Published / RFC Editor Queue:** The hybrid KEM document has been published as an RFC. The ML-KEM and ML-DSA drafts are currently in the RFC Editor queue.
- **Near Last Call:** [draft-ietf-tls-extended-key-update](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-extended-key-update/) and [draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-trust-anchor-ids/) are nearing Working Group Last Call (WGLC).
- **FATT Review:** [draft-ietf-tls-pake](https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-pake/) requires Formally Verified Automated Analysis and Testing (FATT) review before advancing.
